{
  "id": "semantic_tokens/lexical/12_format_strings",
  "topic": "semantic_tokens",
  "subtopic": "lexical",
  "title": "Format strings",
  "summary": "The placeholders of a format string are `formatSpecifier` tokens",
  "prose": "A string passed where a function takes a format string — a\n`basic_format_string` parameter as `std::format`, `std::print` and {fmt}\ndeclare it, or the argument a `format(printf, …)` attribute names — splits\ninto its text and its placeholders: `{}` and `{:>8.2f}` in the first style,\n`%d` and `%-8.3f` in printf's. Escaped braces and `%%` stay text, and so does\na string no function reads as a format.",
  "status": "supported",
  "issues": [],
  "files": [
    {
      "path": "fmt.h",
      "text": "#pragma once\n\nnamespace fmt {\n\ntemplate <class T>\nstruct type_identity {\n    using type = T;\n};\n\ntemplate <class... Args>\nstruct basic_format_string {\n    consteval basic_format_string(const char* text) : text(text) {}\n\n    const char* text;\n};\n\ntemplate <class... Args>\nusing format_string = basic_format_string<typename type_identity<Args>::type...>;\n\ntemplate <class... Args>\nvoid print(format_string<Args...> format, Args&&... args) {}\n\n}  // namespace fmt\n\n[[gnu::format(printf, 1, 2)]] int log_line(const char* format, ...);\n",
      "markers": []
    },
    {
      "path": "main.cpp",
      "text": "#include \"fmt.h\"\n\nvoid report(int count, double ratio, const char* name) {\n    fmt::print(\"{} items, {:>8.2f} ratio, {{braces}}\\n\", count, ratio);\n    log_line(\"%s: %d of %-8.3f%%\\n\", name, count, ratio);\n    const char* plain = \"{} stays text\";\n}\n",
      "markers": []
    }
  ],
